  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nMid and upper level low to track thru the Great Lakes tonight and \ninto New England Saturday. This will place the Ohio Valley in a\nnorthwest flow pattern. At the surface a secondary cold front pushed\nthru the area this morning. In the wake of this front temperatures \nwill drop to the low to mid 30s tonight. Have continued the frost\nadvisory across the southern counties. Surface high pressure builds\ninto the Lower MS Valley Saturday/Saturday night. Considerable \nclouds - especially across the north will diminish late in the day\ninto Saturday evening. Decreasing winds combined with clear skies \nwill lead to cool overnight temperatures. Expect lows generally in\nthe lower 30s with some cooler valleys bottoming out in the upper\n20s. Some minor moderation to temperatures Sunday night but still \ncool with lows in the lower and middle 30s. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nA dry forecast is expected through most of next week as northwest \nflow aloft becomes more westerly. High temperatures in the upper 50s\nand lower 60s Monday warm into the middle 60s Tuesday. A short wave\nto dig southeast across the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley Thursday and\nFriday. This system will bring the next chance for rain and offer\ncooler temperatures with highs in the lower and middle 50s for Friday\nand Saturday and lows in the lower 30s.",
